WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:04.940
In chapter 5 of One Piece, Zoro officially
accepted Luffy’s offer to join the crew.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:10.210
And in only two years, this partnership would
lead them to become two of the strongest fighters

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.920
in the entire world.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.650
But what if Zoro rejected Luffy’s offer
and never joined the straw hat crew?

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.720
Just how far would Luffy get on this journey?

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.199
And before we jump into changes in the story,
let’s actually take a look at the moment

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:27.580
that inspired this whole video, when Luffy
first invited Zoro to join the crew.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:33.420
At this point, Zoro was tied to a post for
saving this little girl from these bad doggos.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.690
Luffy then invited him to become the very
first crew member.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:40.470
And you might not remember, but Zoro initially
refused.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:45.140
However, when Luffy recovered his swords and
then freed the green moss head from his ropes,

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.360
he finally agreed to join the crew.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:52.840
But obviously for this video, le’ts assume
that Zoro rejects Luffy a second time, slapping

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:56.320
away his invitation like a follow request
from a creepy stranger.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:01.340
And if this were the case, Luffy could leave
Zoro tied up which would lead to him actually

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:03.359
being executed by the marines.

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:08.909
But honestly, another much more likely scenario
is that Luffy would still set Zoro free because

00:01:08.909 --> 00:01:11.680
he knows deep down that Zoro is a good person.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:16.700
So after defeating the marines, Zoro would
thank Luffy, but then simply walk away and

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:21.150
pursue his dream of becoming the world’s
strongest swordsman on his own.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:25.500
And this will have massive consequences in
almost every part of the story.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:29.810
Because as we see all throughout the story
and this video, when Luffy is on his own he

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:32.000
usually finds a way to get himself almost
killed.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.000
*Wow*.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.250
How is this guy going to become pirate king
anyway?

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:39.549
But now without Zoro, let's start with Wano
Country.

00:01:39.549 --> 00:01:40.549
Wait… what?

00:01:40.549 --> 00:01:42.439
Why are we starting so late in the story?

00:01:42.439 --> 00:01:45.980
Well, since the point of this video is to
see how far the Straw Hats would get without

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:50.100
Zoro, it made sense to me to start at the
end and work our way backwards.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:54.890
So we’ll be examining each of Zoro’s important
moments in the story and then seeing how things

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:58.159
would be different without him.

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:03.469
And because we are going in reverse order,
there won’t be any major storyline changes

00:02:03.469 --> 00:02:05.280
like some of my previous what if videos.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:10.270
So before we look at all of Zoro’s legendary
battles later on, let’s start early in the

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:11.550
arc.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:16.730
He did have minor fights, like against this
straw man and in the battle to stop this former

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:21.160
daimyo's execution but in each of these conflicts
there were other straw hat’s present who

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.210
could’ve easily performed the same roles.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:28.550
And not even counting the battles, his history
as a descendant of Wano literally never played

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:35.330
a role in the story, so even if he wasn’t
here the crew would’ve been just as motivated

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:36.400
to fight Kaido.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.720
And this takes us to the climactic battles
of Onigashima.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:44.740
Here Zoro was a major participant in the rooftop
battle against Big Mom and Kaido.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:47.530
And his presence was definitely felt here.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:52.390
He got in a few attacks, and blocked one of
the strongest attacks we have seen in the

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:53.800
entire story.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:59.739
But ultimately, this battle was never really
decided either way, so did he really make

00:02:59.739 --> 00:03:01.470
that big of a difference???

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:02.470
**shrug**

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:06.540
But next was his truly epic battle against
Kaido’s right hand man, King.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:15.010
And while this was an incredibly hyped battle,
there are other characters nearby who probably

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:17.940
could’ve fought King as well.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:23.069
In particular, Marco the Phoenix was not doing
much at all during this fight, so he could’ve

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:25.569
been a perfect match to fight the flying dinosaur.

00:03:25.569 --> 00:03:30.900
Likewise, Luffy could have handled King no
problem once he was done with Kaido.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:41.989
So as disappointing as it may sound, the straw
hats ultimately would have been fine in Wano

00:03:41.989 --> 00:03:43.129
even without Zoro.

00:03:43.129 --> 00:03:50.409
But I can promise you that will not be the
case for some of the arcs later on in the

00:03:50.409 --> 00:03:51.409
story.

00:03:51.409 --> 00:03:55.310
But since Zoro wasn’t in Whole Cake Island
at all, we’ll move ahead to Zou.

00:03:55.310 --> 00:04:00.670
And on the back of this giant elephant, Zoro’s
fighting abilities weren’t really needed.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:06.549
However, he did demonstrate one of his other
super important roles on the crew: his leadership.

00:04:06.549 --> 00:04:10.099
When Sanji left to take care of his family
problems, Zoro told the rest of the crew that

00:04:10.099 --> 00:04:12.989
Sanji better damn well apologize for his actions.

00:04:12.989 --> 00:04:17.299
He left the crew at a super important time
in the story plus he was going to stir up

00:04:17.299 --> 00:04:19.410
trouble with a second emperor.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:24.190
And Zoro’s role here is important because
he is the only one who will really step up

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:27.120
and demand respect for the crew and its captain.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:32.470
And while this tense moment didn’t result
in any major conflict, it was a good reminder

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:35.760
for Luffy about the honor and respect needed
on the crew.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:40.050
But even if Zoro wasn’t here to give that
reminder, I don’t think it would have changed

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.810
Luffy’s actions much in Whole Cake Island.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:47.490
However, that is definitely not the case for
another important moment coming up for the

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.280
crew later on.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:55.200
So three arcs down and the Straw Hats would’ve
been just fine in each one.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.200
Interesting…

00:04:56.200 --> 00:05:01.169
Maybe one day if Zoro’s sense of direction
really got him lost, the crew would be just

00:05:01.169 --> 00:05:02.169
fine.

00:05:02.169 --> 00:05:08.130
But this brings us to Dressrosa, where Zoro
fought and defeated this giant stone man.

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:13.370
However, this is another enemy who isn’t
really all that powerful – I mean how could

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:22.370
he be with a voice like that – so someone
like Law, Sabo, or Luffy could have defeated

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:27.210
Pika almost instantly.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:34.370
Moving back even further, Zoro does have a
moment in Punk Hazard when he yells at Luffy

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:36.880
after his captain almost died at the hands
of this gas man.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.280
He demands that Luffy take things more seriously
and reminds them that they are in the most

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:40.930
dangerous part of the world now.

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:45.840
Of course, Luffy laughs it off so maybe it
wouldn’t matter even if Zoro was here to

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:47.870
remind his captain not to mess around.

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:52.990
Zoro also defeated this snow bird lady but
someone else could’ve easily taken her down

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:53.990
as well.

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:57.870
And this is going to bring us all the way
back to the time skip.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:03.960
So as you can see, Zoro’s influence in the
post-time skip was not as important as you

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.870
might have previously thought.

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:10.740
And that’s because even though Zoro has
a fight in basically every arc, the crew is

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:17.060
not majorly challenged like they were in the
pre-time skip.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:23.360
Plus everyone else is now super strong, so
Zoro isn’t one of the only strong fighters

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:24.360
in the crew.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:28.940
Buuuutt, things are going to be way different
the further back we get in the story.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:33.130
However, Zoro doesn’t play any role in the
events leading up to Marineford.

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:38.900
And even though straw hats were defeated on
Sabaody, Zoro’s absence wouldn’t really

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:41.960
have a major effect on the outcome anyway.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:47.590
Now traveling back in time, let’s discuss
the nightmare-island, Thriller Bark, where

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:53.289
Zoro has HIS MOST BADASS MOMENT in the entire
story.

00:06:53.289 --> 00:07:00.970
In his first fight of the arc, Zoro defeats
this zombie swordsman.

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:05.050
But I definitely think that Nightmare Luffy
could have also defeated the samurai.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:09.460
But the even greater conflict came at the
end of the arc, when Zoro stood up to the

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:11.560
warlord Kuma to save Luffy.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:16.250
In exchange for Luffy’s life, Zoro agreed
to take on all of his captain’s pain from

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:17.250
the previous battle.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:22.341
And this resulted in the famous “Nothing
Happened” scene, which is personally one

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:24.550
of my favorites in the entire story.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:30.400
But with Zoro not on the crew, it would fall
to Sanji to take on his captain’s pain.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:35.099
I mean, Sanji already wanted to do this anyway
but Zoro knocked him aside.

00:07:35.099 --> 00:07:40.720
So in this case, Sanji takes on all of the
pain, and we seriously have ask if he would

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:44.660
be able to survive this ordeal.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:51.280
And Sanji stans don’t hate me, but I honestly
think the answer is no.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:56.180
Zoro is shown all throughout the story to
have crazy endurance and the ability to fight

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:57.180
through pain.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:03.240
So even though we have recently learned more
about Sanji's incredible body, I don’t think

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:07.220
that he could survive this crazy amount of
damage.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:09.330
So sorry, Sanji…

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:13.280
Looks like you needed your moss head friend
after all.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:17.360
But since we are now getting to the points
in the story where Zoro is absolutely needed,

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:20.080
I do want to add one major disclaimer.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:24.110
Even though there will be a bunch of points
where Luffy would fail without Zoro, we can

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:28.690
usually find a reason for the straw hats to
continue.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:33.220
For example, in this situation with Kuma,
it is possible the warlord takes mercy on

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:36.160
them because he is friends with Luffy’s
father after all.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:42.399
So while we can usually find an excuse, there
are some arcs that are just impossible to

00:08:42.399 --> 00:08:44.459
move on from without Zoro.

00:08:44.459 --> 00:08:49.410
And this brings us to the government’s judicial
island, Enies Lobby.

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:55.990
During this arc, we see one of the three major
characteristics that Zoro brings to the crew.

00:08:55.990 --> 00:09:02.120
Two of these we will discuss coming up very
soon, but the first characteristic is that

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:05.250
he is just a badass fighter.

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:10.310
At this point in the story, he, Luffy, and
Sanji are the only strong ones who can really

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:13.390
fight – no offense Nami and Robin.

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:16.390
And Chopper loses his mind when he goes berserk.

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:23.050
So Zoro’s absence is a major problem when
Luffy is somehow distracted or taken out because

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:26.370
then there is no one left to protect the others.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:30.400
And this situation happens in basically every
arc.

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:34.520
But maybe that means that Luffy would take
things more seriously, so he doesn’t put

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:36.740
the rest of the crew in danger.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:37.740
Buuut…

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:38.930
I kinda doubt it.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:43.130
So let’s keep this in mind as we shift back
to Zoro’s fight against this sword-wielding

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:44.130
giraffe.

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:49.360
Zoro eventually wins this battle and claims
key number 5 which is the exact key needed

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:55.110
to free Robin from her handcuffs, so without
Zoro winning this fight, Robin would be trapped

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:56.110
for good.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:10:01.840
However, I do think someone else like Luffy
or Sanji could have defeated the giraffe man,

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:20.310
so in the end Robin 

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:54.709
would 

00:10:54.709 --> 00:11:07.339
still be free.

00:11:07.339 --> 00:11:18.500
However, moving back to Water 7, we get another
critical example of how without Zoro’s presence

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:23.130
as the unofficial Vice-Captain, the crew would
surely fall apart.

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:26.070
So the crew reached Water 7 in need of a new
ship.

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:31.220
This of course sparks the fierce duel between
Usopp and Luffy, which results in Usopp leaving

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:32.370
the crew.

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:36.260
And this is an incredibly important moment
for the crew’s long term future.

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:40.899
And that’s BECAUSE IF Luffy gave in to Usopp’s
demands, it would have shown the crew that

00:11:40.899 --> 00:11:45.800
Luffy is not a strong captain and he is not
worthy of their faith.

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:53.820
However, in chapter 333, Zoro will not let
Luffy take the easy route and he reminds Luffy

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:58.380
that making these difficult choices are the
burden of being the captain.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:03.829
But without Zoro in this scene, Luffy may
very well have chosen to keep Usopp’s friendship

00:12:03.829 --> 00:12:06.120
rather than do what was best for the crew.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:11.430
And if Luffy let Usopp rejoin the crew or
agreed to keep using their ship, it could

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:14.449
have disastrous consequences later on.

00:12:14.449 --> 00:12:21.010
For example, if they did keep using the Merry,
it could have sunk in the middle of the ocean.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:25.430
Or if Luffy didn’t earn the respect of the
crew in this scene, they may not always listen

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:26.930
to his orders later on.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:31.779
And this lack of respect and leadership could
eventually lead to a tragic breakup during

00:12:31.779 --> 00:12:33.470
some future conflict.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:39.230
So here we have our first true example of
Zoro’s importance to the crew.

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:43.480
Because I really don’t think that anyone
else on the crew is as serious and devoted

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:47.190
to respect to have the same kind of impact
as Vice-Captain.

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:50.380
Sanji is kinda wishy-washy.

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:53.279
Usopp has his moments, but is too weak.

00:12:53.279 --> 00:12:57.180
And Nami would rather avoid these kinds of
serious issues within the crew.

00:12:57.180 --> 00:13:02.120
And besides his fighting and leadership qualities,
there is even a third characteristic that

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:04.949
no one else on the crew possesses.

00:13:04.949 --> 00:13:11.040
Out of all the straw hats, Zoro is the one
most single-mindedly focused on his goal of

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:14.170
becoming the world’s strongest swordsmen.

00:13:14.170 --> 00:13:17.639
It is pretty much the easiest goal to understand.

00:13:17.639 --> 00:13:22.570
It probably sounds a little bit like this
in Zoro’s mind: Get stronger.

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.660
Defeat enemies.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:27.649
Simple, right?

00:13:27.649 --> 00:13:32.830
But Zoro is also the only one we consistently
see training to reach his goals.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:38.060
He is frequently lifting weights or practicing
his sword skills, and I like to think that

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:40.339
this has some effect on the crew as well.

00:13:40.339 --> 00:13:44.420
So we have to wonder if losing Zoro would
make the crew less dedicated towards their

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:45.420
goals.

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:49.460
I think Luffy would still of course want to
be pirate king, but as you’ll see in just

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:53.970
a moment, Zoro’s was truly irreplaceable
in the early parts of the story.

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:57.240
Plus, if Zoro’s not there to butt heads
with Sanji, then the cook’s pervertedness

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:59.820
might reach even more ridiculous heights.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:04.670
Who knows Nami could even kill Sanji herself
if he peeps in on her bath one too many times.

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:10.199
But now onto Skypiea, where Zoro plays a key
role in the outcome of the arc His first major

00:14:10.199 --> 00:14:13.029
action was when he defeated this winged puppy
lover.

00:14:13.029 --> 00:14:17.339
And while there was no one else around to
really take this guy out, I can imagine Luffy

00:14:17.339 --> 00:14:19.990
defeating him pretty easily once he got out
of the snake.

00:14:19.990 --> 00:14:25.140
And after this, none of the surviving characters
can defeat the lightning god Enel, so Zoro

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:29.060
basically takes a nap until he helps cut down
the giant beanstalk.

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:34.240
So without Zoro it is possible the beanstalk
never gets cut down, which means Luffy would

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:37.759
have not reached Enel in time to deliver the
final blow.

00:14:37.759 --> 00:14:44.780
But I think between this warrior’s dedication
and Nami’s cleverness, they would have found

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:46.560
some way to get Luffy to Enel.

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:51.730
But this brings us to Alabasta and the juicy
bits of this video.

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:56.389
Zoro’s main role in the arc is to take down
the warlord Crocodile’s right hand man,

00:14:56.389 --> 00:14:57.389
Mr. 1.

00:14:57.389 --> 00:15:02.430
And originally, this was a huge moment of
growth for Zoro as he finally learned how

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:03.650
to cut steel.

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:08.820
Kinda crazy, actually that he couldn’t even
do that up until this point in the story.

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:15.019
But with Zoro out of the picture, someone
else needs to stop this insane blade man from

00:15:15.019 --> 00:15:16.410
tearing through the crew.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:20.690
Certainly, I think Luffy could eventually
figure out a way to beat Mr. 1, even though

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:25.010
Luffy and sharp things don’t get along too
well.

00:15:25.010 --> 00:15:29.810
But Luffy already had his hands full with
Crocodile, so someone else would need to take

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:35.010
out Mr. 1 or distract Croc-man – or mom
– while Luffy takes out Mr. Blades.

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:40.240
And I think their best chance is a combination
of Sanji and Nami, where Sanji could keep

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:49.060
Mr. 1 busy while Nami figures out how to strike
him with lightning.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:53.870
But that’s not the only critical role Zoro
plays.

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:58.110
He is also part of the team that helps Vivi
reach the bomb, and without Zoro to fling

00:15:58.110 --> 00:16:01.690
Chopper and Vivi into the air, they would
have to come up with another plan to reach

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:02.690
the top.

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:08.899
Perhaps Usopp could quickly make a giant slingshot,
or another option is the marine captain Smoker

00:16:08.899 --> 00:16:15.940
could help by using his Smoke logia powers
to get them up to the bomb.

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:20.990
And you might be asking why would Smoker help
them out, but I certainly don’t think the

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:26.190
marine captain would just stand around if
he knew that millions could die from a giant

00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:27.190
bomb.

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:31.100
Plus these are desperate times without our
favorite swordsman, so we’ve gotta be a

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:34.300
little creative here.

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:38.089
So after Luffy defeats Crocodile, the straw
hats get their next major bounties.

00:16:38.089 --> 00:16:43.639
And without Zoro to take much of the credit,
the rest of the straw hats get a pretty good

00:16:43.639 --> 00:16:45.319
bump in each of their bounties.

00:16:45.319 --> 00:16:51.649
Which is great for Sanji, Usopp, and maybe
Chopper finally gets the respect he deserves,

00:16:51.649 --> 00:16:54.870
but Nami is certainly not pleased with this
turn of events.

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:59.660
So as punishment, she demands that you subscribe
to the channel for more one piece content

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:00.890
just like this.

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:06.530
Let’s jump out of the desert now, and continue
moving backwards.

00:17:06.530 --> 00:17:12.089
Certainly, the straw hats would be just fine
in Little Garden and Drum Island, since Zoro

00:17:12.089 --> 00:17:17.510
basically just got stuck in wax and then decided
to have a little winter time workout in the

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:18.510
snow.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:22.230
But this brings us to the booze-lovers favorite
island, Whiskey Peak.

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:26.510
Here the straw hats were tricked into passing
out drunk and then the entire island tried

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:28.870
to capture them to earn bounty money.

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:34.970
However, Zoro was sober enough to fight them
off until Luffy and the others woke up.

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:39.910
So while Zoro did a lot of work here, none
of these enemies were super powerful, so I

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:43.710
think Luffy and the others would have eventually
gotten free no matter what.

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:49.169
So as hard as it is to believe, over nine
hundred chapters in reverse and we’ve only

00:17:49.169 --> 00:17:54.289
had one real moment where Zoro’s absence
could have led to an eventual break up, and

00:17:54.289 --> 00:17:59.360
a few others that required creative solutions
for the crew to advance.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:02.150
But no absolute crushing defeats.

00:18:02.150 --> 00:18:03.860
And next is the East Blue!

00:18:03.860 --> 00:18:05.280
The weakest Sea of all.

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:09.100
It should be a walk in the park for the straw
hats… right?

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:10.100
Right???

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:13.370
Well, let’s see if they can survive Arlong
Park.

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:16.780
Here the straw hats will again be missing
Zoro’s fierce loyalty to the crew.

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:21.620
Because in chapter 71, Zoro confronts Nami
in front of this gang of Fishmen.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:25.690
And here Nami is still pretending that she
doesn’t care about the crew, but Zoro does

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:27.830
not believe her AT ALL.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:33.220
In fact, to prove that she still belongs with
the crew, he throws himself into the water.

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:37.640
This forces Nami to choose to let him drown
or save him herself.

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:44.170
Of course Nami saves him, which proves to
both Zoro AND Nami that she still cares about

00:18:44.170 --> 00:18:45.429
the crew.

00:18:45.429 --> 00:18:50.260
So without Zoro here, this entire arc could
play out very differently.

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:54.330
Nami may not be as convinced about her true
feelings for the straw hats, or at least it

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:57.600
may take her longer to finally break down
and accept help.

00:18:57.600 --> 00:19:02.470
But beyond the emotional stakes, Zoro also
played a significant role in the fights in

00:19:02.470 --> 00:19:03.490
Arlong Park.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:07.900
Because even though he was still seriously
injured from his early battles – more on

00:19:07.900 --> 00:19:13.600
that very soon – he fought off this sword-wielding
octopus and even kept the fishman’s captain

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:16.200
Arlong busy when Luffy was trapped underwater.

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:21.340
So without Zoro, someone else like Sanji would
need to step in to fight Arlong until Luffy

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:22.340
was rescued.

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:28.210
And this presents all kinds of major challenges,
since Sanji was the one to fight who broke

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:29.750
the rock Luffy was trapped in.

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:35.200
So either someone else would have to keep
Arlong busy – sorry Usopp – or someone

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:39.600
else would need to free Luffy, but I truly
don’t know who else here is strong enough

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:40.760
to do that.

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:46.090
So again, this is our first clear example
where Luffy could have very easily died without

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:47.490
Zoro’s help.

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:53.030
But let’s imagine that Sanji does fight
off Arlong long enough for Luffy to be freed

00:19:53.030 --> 00:19:57.280
by Usopp, who heroically blasts the rock off
of Luffy’s legs with a cannon.

00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:05.010
So with Luffy free, he can defeat Arlong and
rescue Nami’s village for good.

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:10.059
Another narrow escape, but the same cannot
be said of the Baratie, where there is literally

00:20:10.059 --> 00:20:12.870
nothing the straw hats can do on their own
to survive.

00:20:12.870 --> 00:20:14.550
But let’s not get ahead of ourselves.

00:20:14.550 --> 00:20:19.159
First, it is possible that they will never
find Sanji’s floating restaurant at all.

00:20:19.159 --> 00:20:23.860
Because in chapter 42, the straw hat’s new
ship is attacked by everyone’s favorite

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:26.350
bounty hunters, Johnny and Yosaku.

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:30.550
Luffy is ready to kick them off the ship,
but then Zoro recognizes Johnny and they quickly

00:20:30.550 --> 00:20:32.880
become friends and get directions to the Baratie.

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:36.970
However if Zoro was not on board, Luffy might’ve
just thrown them overboard.

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:41.860
This could lead to them never finding the
Baratie, which of course means no Sanji.

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:46.350
However, there are some other possibilities
that could still lead them to Sanji.

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:50.732
First, Luffy might want to recruit these bounty
hunting bros since he still needs a strong

00:20:50.732 --> 00:20:51.732
fighter.

00:20:51.732 --> 00:20:55.210
Or even if he doesn’t they could find out
about the floating restaurant from someone

00:20:55.210 --> 00:20:56.480
else on another island.

00:20:56.480 --> 00:21:02.900
So let’s assume that they just find the
Baratie somehow, where they are 100% going

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:05.340
to be destroyed without Zoro.

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:09.669
And after destroying part of the restaurant,
Luffy is forced to work as a chore boy to

00:21:09.669 --> 00:21:10.669
pay off the damage.

00:21:10.669 --> 00:21:15.610
That is until this pirate commodore eventually
shows up and starts shooting up the place.

00:21:15.610 --> 00:21:18.140
And Zoro’s role in this fight is basically
zero.

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:23.640
However, when the world’s strongest swordsman,
Mihawk, makes his appearance things completely

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:24.640
change.

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:29.080
You see, originally, Mihawk came to the restaurant
intent on taking down the very same pirates

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:30.950
who were now attacking the restaurant.

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:35.779
And after Mihawk easily cuts their giant ship
in half, Zoro steps up to challenge the warlord.

00:21:35.779 --> 00:21:40.330
And even though Zoro is utterly defeated,
Mihawk is so impressed by Zoro’s honor as

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:45.290
a swordsman and his loyalty to Luffy, that
he decides to leave everyone else alone.

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:49.240
And this scene perfectly shows off something
only Zoro brings to the crew.

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:50.929
He is fiercely honorable.

00:21:50.929 --> 00:21:55.559
While Luffy, Nami, and Usopp will use every
trick in the book to defeat an enemy, Zoro

00:21:55.559 --> 00:21:58.330
will face an opponent head on in an honest
duel.

00:21:58.330 --> 00:22:04.090
He is also intensely loyal to the crew, so
much that he places Luffy’s dream’s ahead

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:05.450
of his own.

00:22:05.450 --> 00:22:10.039
And it is these very traits that so inspire
Mihawk to let everyone else live.

00:22:10.039 --> 00:22:14.791
But without Zoro on the crew, there is no
telling what Mihawk would do to the Straw

00:22:14.791 --> 00:22:15.791
Hats.

00:22:15.791 --> 00:22:18.960
Would Mihawk be satisfied just taking this
guy’s head?

00:22:18.960 --> 00:22:19.960
Maybe.

00:22:19.960 --> 00:22:24.480
Or would he want to continue to eliminate
all of the pirates at the restaurant?

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:30.150
And if Mihawk were to come after Luffy, then
our rubber man has absolutely no chance against

00:22:30.150 --> 00:22:32.250
the world’s strongest swordsman.

00:22:32.250 --> 00:22:37.360
So the straw hats’ fate would be entirely
out of their hands.

00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:40.770
But let’s say that Mihawk is feeling generous.

00:22:40.770 --> 00:22:44.909
Or maybe the head chef Zeff convinces him
to spare Luffy because he still needs to work

00:22:44.909 --> 00:22:45.909
off his debt.

00:22:45.909 --> 00:22:49.690
Or, come on let’s be honest, this introvert
just wants to return to his dark castle.

00:22:49.690 --> 00:22:54.980
But without Zoro, this would definitely be
a time the Straw Hats could’ve been wiped

00:22:54.980 --> 00:22:55.980
out.

00:22:55.980 --> 00:22:59.490
And that’s even more true in the arc before
this, Syrup Village.

00:22:59.490 --> 00:23:04.760
So back up to chapter 23, with Luffy, Zoro,
and Nami sailing to Usopp’s home island.

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:09.770
And now that Nami is steering the ship, the
risk of death at sea is basically none.

00:23:09.770 --> 00:23:14.140
So the trio travel to Syrup village, where
they meet the boy who cried wolf, Usopp.

00:23:14.140 --> 00:23:20.279
And Zoro’s role in this arc is minimal until
the final battle, where he fights these feline

00:23:20.279 --> 00:23:21.279
brothers.

00:23:21.279 --> 00:23:25.620
And at this point in the fight, Luffy was
hypnotized and asleep, so unless Nami woke

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:28.640
him up, they would all be in serious trouble.

00:23:28.640 --> 00:23:33.691
So it is entirely possible that the crew is
taken out because Luffy was tricked into a

00:23:33.691 --> 00:23:36.340
situation where he cannot help himself of
the crew.

00:23:36.340 --> 00:23:40.420
*looks down dejectedly* Wow, these guys really
need Zoro.

00:23:40.420 --> 00:23:43.520
But of course, we could imagine that somehow
they make it out alive.

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:48.730
Maybe Luffy never gets put to sleep or that
Nami is able to wake him up earlier.

00:23:48.730 --> 00:23:53.890
Or maybe Usopp shoots him with some smelling
salts – speaking of which, wow those things

00:23:53.890 --> 00:23:54.890
are powerful.

00:23:54.890 --> 00:23:58.750
But with this one I really don’t think they
would have been able to survive.

00:23:58.750 --> 00:24:02.640
I mean without Zoro, Luffy is literally the
only strong fighter.

00:24:02.640 --> 00:24:07.120
So once again, the Straw Hats journey is at
its end.

00:24:07.120 --> 00:24:12.779
But let’s take another step back to Orange
Town, and see how Luffy would do in the first

00:24:12.779 --> 00:24:13.779
arc without Zoro.

00:24:13.779 --> 00:24:16.160
In this small village, Luffy first meets Nami.

00:24:16.160 --> 00:24:20.770
Since Zoro isn’t even on the island yet,
Luffy is still captured by Buggy the Clown.

00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:22.940
So Luffy is locked in a cage.

00:24:22.940 --> 00:24:25.960
He is about to be blasted by Buggy’s special
cannon balls.

00:24:25.960 --> 00:24:30.700
However, in chapter 11, he is saved when Zoro
fights off Buggy and then flips the cannon

00:24:30.700 --> 00:24:31.750
away from Luffy.

00:24:31.750 --> 00:24:35.450
Zoro then carries Luffy’s cage away from
Buggy and into the town.

00:24:35.450 --> 00:24:38.380
However, with no Zoro, Luffy is basically
helpless.

00:24:38.380 --> 00:24:42.220
Nami already tried to save him, but she was
no match against Buggy’s crew.

00:24:42.220 --> 00:24:47.490
So unless Luffy was able to somehow chew his
way out of the cage, his pirate adventure

00:24:47.490 --> 00:24:50.470
is over after just a single island without
Zoro.

00:24:50.470 --> 00:24:51.780
*Take a deep breath.* Damn, that’s actually
kinda sad.

00:24:51.780 --> 00:24:52.890
But all that just proves what Luffy has said
all along.

00:24:52.890 --> 00:24:53.890
He truly wouldn’t be able to do anything
without his crew.

00:24:53.890 --> 00:24:58.149
But while Luffy’s journey without Zoro is
basically over after just one island, that

00:24:58.149 --> 00:25:02.170
means the other straw hats never get to pursue
their dreams as part of the crew.

00:25:02.170 --> 00:25:05.710
And this brings us to an even more interesting
question.

00:25:05.710 --> 00:25:12.000
What would happen to everyone else in the
story, if Luffy was never born?

00:25:12.000 --> 00:25:15.390
And if you want to watch that video, you can
click right here.

00:25:15.390 --> 00:25:17.190
Shanks for watching.

